            <ArticleTitle>Primary renal carcinoid natural history of the disease for ten years: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Primary renal carcinoid is extremely rare and there are few reports on the natural history of the disease.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE PRESENTATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 68-year-old male with a right renal mass who lost to follow-up for ten years has been presented. His only complaint was a mild flank pain. Upon admission to the hospital for his renal mass, he underwent a right radical nephrectomy and pathological examination revealed the diagnosis of primary renal carcinoid.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">In light of the presented case, primary renal carcinoma may have a prolonged natural history with no distant metastasis and any change in the quality of life of the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
